course: dictionary
lesson: 13058
title: Featherless and what it tells us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Featherless is built from two parts: feather and -less. The ending -less means without, so featherless means having no feathers. Other words work the same way: hopeless, careless and spotless.
explain: «The featherless chick sat in the nest, waiting for its mum.» The chick has no feathers yet, so it is still a baby. The clues are chick and nest, which tell you what kind of bird it is and where it is.
explain: «The bird had a featherless patch on its wing after it moulted.» To moult means to lose old feathers before new ones grow. So a featherless patch is a bare spot on the wing where no feathers are growing for now.
fact: Featherless is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a featherless chick.
fact: «Featherless» means having no feathers.
fact: Many newly hatched chicks are featherless and helpless, so they need their parents to care for them.
fact: «A featherless patch» means a bare spot where feathers are missing.
fact: The ending -less means without, so you can work out many words, such as hopeless and careless.
exercise: «The featherless chick peeped loudly in the nest.» What does featherless mean? | *Having no feathers | Singing a happy song | Flying high in the sky | Having very long feathers
exercise: Ben saw a bird with a featherless patch. Where were the feathers missing? | On its beak | On its tail | *On its wing | In its nest
exercise: Copy the word that means having no feathers. | *featherless | bird | nest | sing
test: Which word fits the gap? «The ____ chick was helpless in the nest.» | *featherless | loud | bright | colourful
test: What does «a featherless patch» mean? | *A spot where no feathers grow for now | A mat made of feathers | A patch of soft wool | A spot covered in thick, fluffy feathers
exam: Which of these is featherless? | A duck swimming on the lake | *A newly hatched chick | A blue jay with bright feathers | A peacock with its tail spread wide
